# Data provenance — benchmarks/ask-plan

STATUS: DESIGN, NOTHING MEASURED. This directory ships raw public datasets,
licence notes, and derivation scripts. It contains zero measured numbers; every
F1 / token / latency figure in the README is a gate definition, not a result.

## What is here

| dataset | index the harness builds | docs | raw file | sha256 (first 16) |
|---|---|---:|---|---|
| usgs-earthquakes | `ax-usgs-earthquakes` | 655 | `raw/usgs-earthquakes/usgs-earthquakes.csv` | `2f52fcc27e5e199b` |
| nasa-exoplanets | `ax-nasa-exoplanets` | 3,000 | `raw/nasa-exoplanets/nasa-exoplanets.csv` | `2d18679052b6c876` |
| gapminder | `ax-gapminder` | 1,704 | `raw/gapminder/gapminder.tsv` | `f74275b4a2f4a7c8` |

All three were downloaded from this sandbox on 2026-09-29 (UTC) (HTTP 200, full
body); the pinned URLs and full sha256s live in each directory's
`provenance.json` and are re-checked by `scripts/fetch_data.py --check`.
Licences: [usgs-earthquakes](./raw/usgs-earthquakes/LICENCE) (USGS public
domain), [nasa-exoplanets](./raw/nasa-exoplanets/LICENCE) (NASA public
domain by statute + requested acknowledgment, no explicit licence statement on
the service pages — read the caveat there),
[gapminder](./raw/gapminder/LICENCE) (CC BY 4.0). All three permit
redistribution; the USGS and Gapminder credits are printed in their licence
notes as requested.

**Why the raw files are committed:** gold result sets must be reproducible from
pinned bytes. Both upstreams move (the exoplanet composite table refreshes
monthly; USGS revises historical windows as solutions improve), so the committed
snapshot — not the live URL — is the canonical input to
`scripts/derive_pairs.py`. `scripts/fetch_data.py` exists to re-acquire and to
report drift, not to redefine gold.

## Rejected during acquisition (and why, for the record)

- SSA baby names (`ssa.gov/oact/babynames/names.zip`) — HTTP 403 from this
  sandbox.
- NHTSA recalls flat file (`static.nhtsa.gov/.../FLAT_RCL.zip`) — HTTP 404.
- BLS CPI series (`download.bls.gov`) — HTTP 403.

These were rejected on reachability, not licence; none is redistributed here.

## Layout

```
data/
  raw/<dataset>/            committed upstream snapshot + LICENCE + provenance.json
  gold/pairs.jsonl          >= 200 (prompt, gold result set) pairs — GENERATED,
                            deterministically, by scripts/derive_pairs.py; never
                            edited by hand and never derived from an engine
  gold/negative-prompts.jsonl  prompts naming values that do NOT exist in the data;
                            #1056 says these must 422 naming the phrase. Not counted
                            in the 200; DESIGN only.
```
